{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1464944-how-well-could-this-work-in-deviant","id":1464944,"title":"How well could this work in Deviant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-22T17:47:20-07:00","id":1464944,"title":"How well could this work in Deviant","content":"I am thinking about purchasing Deviant soon and am already planning a Chronicle to run with it. One idea I had for this Chronicle was to include a group besides the Conspiracies to go after said Deviants.The idea i eventually rested on is a group similar to such real life groups like MUFON and The Society for Psychical Research. They believe that Deviants are actually beings from a different world, or planes of existence and wish to study them and their &quot;unique physiological and psychological differences&quot;, and discount any &quot;rubbish&quot; they spout about conspiracies as just their nerves being frayed from their journey to Earth. To this end, they end up sending operatives out into the world to investigate, seek out, and ultimately capture Deviants and bring them back for testing, interviews, and light experimentation, a fate not so different from the Deviant's past.<br /> <br /> Could these fellows work in the Deviant splat and can I have some advice on making them interesting antagonists to tackle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:17:40-07:00","id":1464953,"title":"","content":"I think that'd work fine for a Deviant game, though ultimately within the framework of the rules such a group would act as a Conspiracy. Rappelle-toi that a Conspiracy is simply a group of individuals working together toward a common cause; all that stuff about barbarism is simply Renegade delusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T20:04:38-07:00","id":1464958,"title":"","content":"Deviant, while it has some flexibility based on how many Scars you start your characters with, is overall a lower-powered game that's already calibrated to favor having a lot of ordinary human antagonists. The group you've described is a perfectly valid concept for a Deviant conspiracy. While the &quot;archetypal&quot; conspiracy is often assumed to be engaged in triggering the Divergence, that's not a requirement and a conspiracy doesn't have to have any supernatural capabilities at all.<br /> <br /> You could even run a cohort of entirely Accidental Remade and have a game where <i>nobody</i> knows how to deliberately trigger Divergence and there don't exist any conspiracies responsible for transforming the player characters. What's important for a game of Deviant is having a dramatic vendetta against an organized opposition.<br /> <br /> Your antagonists would still be wrong in discounting deviants as having a delusion of conspiratorial oppression. They are, after all, being oppressed by a conspiracy aligned against them: this conspiracy, the one the antagonists are in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}